WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.434
-Last night, voters in Kansas
overwhelmingly rejected

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.834
a state ballot measure

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.567
that would have restricted
abortion access

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.367
despite shady GOP tactics.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:12.267
And Donald Trump endorsed
multiple dudes named Eric

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.834
in the same Senate race
in Missouri.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:16.267
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.367
There was a huge victory

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.400
for reproductive rights
last night in Kansas,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.200
where a proposed amendment
to that state's Constitution

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.934
that would have removed
abortion protections

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:32.634
was rejected overwhelmingly
by voters.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:35.567
-There is big news
on this big primary night.

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:39.000
NBC News projects voters
in the state of Kansas

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.901
have overwhelmingly voted

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.200
to keep the protection
of abortion rights

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.067
in their state Constitution.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:48.634
This was the first test of
the right to choose at the polls

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:51.334
since the Supreme Court
ended Roe vs. Wade.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.534
-Wow. Somewhere right now,
Brett Kavanaugh is angrily

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:56.467
chugging a Coors Light tall boy
with PJ &amp; Squi.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:59.200
I'm sure he's making that face,
you know?

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.167
He really manages to
look incredibly angry

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.767
and incredibly goofy
at the same time,

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:05.767
like a Chihuahua who
just saw the mailman.

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:09.000
This is obviously
encouraging news

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.300
in the fight to safeguard access
to abortion,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.033
and it's especially encouraging

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:15.000
given that
anti-abortion activists

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.834
used every shady tactic they
could think of and still lost.

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:20.968
For example, the wording
of the ballot question

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:23.300
was intentionally designed to
be as confusing as possible.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.968
Now, if the measure had passed,

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.634
it would have removed
abortion protections

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:29.300
and allow the GOP legislature
to ban abortion.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.300
But the wording of the language
was intentionally confusing.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.634
Here it is, quote...

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.234
Man, I can't believe
they hired the same guy

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.567
who wrote
the iTunes user agreement.

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:10.601
I hope voters were given the
options "yes," "no," or [bleep]

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:12.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:15.701
That reads like the intro
to a college paper

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:19.267
you start writing at 3:00 a.m.
the night before it's due.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:01.868
[ Applause, cheering ]

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:05.968
Thankfully, Kansas voters
saw through the bull[bleep]

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.901
and overwhelmingly
backed abortion rights

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:10.434
even though a shady GOP group
also sent out

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.534
a bunch of misleading
text messages on Monday

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:15.434
suggesting that voting yes
on the proposed amendment

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:17.000
would have protected
reproductive rights,

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.901
when, in reality, it would have
done the exact opposite.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:22.834
-In Kansas, where that critical
abortion access vote

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:25.434
is happening right now,
voters across the state

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:28.567
received this misleading
text message yesterday.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.167
Quote...

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:43.267
That is not true.

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:46.067
The measure on the ballot
does not protect choice.

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:48.801
In fact, it would change
the state Constitution

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:51.334
and do the exact opposite.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.434
-You know, as a general rule,
if your best strategy

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:55.968
is to try to trick people into
accidentally voting for you,

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.834
that's probably a sign
that you're the bad guys.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:59.567
It's like, if in order
to get people

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:00.934
to watch this show online,

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:02.868
we made the title
of every YouTube video

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.033
"Click Here
for Free Boner Pills"...

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:07.501
Although if you fall for that,
shame on you

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:10.334
because the free ones
don't work.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.801
Fellas, you got
to listen to me here.

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:14.767
I know you're thinking, "If I
can get the pills for free,

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:16.467
I can splash out
on a romantic dinner,

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:18.100
the horse and buggy
through Central Park."

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.434
But none of that's
going to matter

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.133
when you pop one
of the freebies and realize

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:22.534
that was definitely a Skittle.

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:26.534
There are things in life
worth paying for,

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:28.801
which is why the only
erectile-dysfunction e-mail

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:29.834
you should ever open is

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.701
Boner Pills --
Reasonably Priced.

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:37.200
And I know this from experience
because a friend told it to me.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:40.767
But that was not the only
bizarre subterfuge

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.467
on display
from Republicans yesterday.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.300
In fact, in another state,
Missouri Republicans

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.434
tried something even dumber.

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.334
In fact, this is a story
that I think pretty much

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:49.434
perfectly captures the current
state of the Republican Party.

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:51.767
Donald Trump, a man who,
let's not forget,

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.133
tried to overthrow
American democracy

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:55.100
and is currently under multiple
criminal investigations,

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.767
created confusion in Missouri's
Republican Senate primary

00:04:57.767 --> 00:05:00.267
by endorsing
someone named Eric

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:02.400
in a race with multiple Eric's

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.200
without specifying which Eric
he was endorsing.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.033
And then both Erics bragged

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.067
that they'd been endorsed
by Trump,

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:13.033
a man who, again,
is not only under multiple

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:15.033
active criminal investigations
for inciting a coup

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.467
to overthrow American democracy,

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:19.467
but is also beginning to look
less like a former president

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:23.133
and more like
the Nick Nolte mug shot.

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:26.267
I mean, is his head
getting smaller,

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.968
or is his hat getting bigger?

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.968
It looks like his hat
is some kind of organism

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:32.033
feeding on his blood.

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.767
Look how pale he is.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:35.667
He looks like he's starring
in the next Martin McDonagh film

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:38.501
as the ghost of an Irish priest
opposite Colin Farrell.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.634
Look, I know.

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:44.534
I know they say
all presidents age rapidly,

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:46.100
but Trump looks like
he's halfway through

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:49.601
a "Raiders of the Lost Ark"
face melt.

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:52.133
It's like he opened the ark,
his face started to melt,

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:54.367
but then he slammed it shut
real fast.

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:55.901
But then his face
just stayed that way.

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:58.100
"The ark of the covenant --
we love the ark.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.100
We love the ark, don't we folks?

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:03.267
They told me not to open it,
but we had to open it.

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:05.667
Many people are saying the ark,

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.734
that's where they hid
Hunter Biden's laptop.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:10.300
And then -- And then
I open it up,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.434
and the ghosts -- the ghosts
started pouring out.

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:13.901
They poured out, the ghosts.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:18.300
And that -- that's how I
ended up hiring my lawyer."

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.901
Anyway, that dude --
that dude right there --

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:25.400
that dude endorsed two Erics,
two Eric's in the same race.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.033
And then they both
debased themselves

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:30.467
by scrambling to claim
that endorsement.

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:32.434
-Just a short time ago,
the former president offered

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:35.300
his endorsement in a key
Senate race in Missouri.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.734
He endorsed Eric,

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:38.567
leaving it open for voters
to choose

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:40.667
between the two Erics
who are actually in the race,

00:06:40.667 --> 00:06:42.934
one of whom, the former
Governor Eric Greitens,

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:46.234
resigned from office four years
ago after a sex scandal

00:06:46.234 --> 00:06:48.000
and is now facing
allegations of abuse

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.133
from his ex-wife,
which he denies.

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:51.968
-Former President Trump
announced

00:06:51.968 --> 00:06:55.734
his long-awaited endorsement
late yesterday afternoon,

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:59.834
saying, "I trust the great
people of Missouri on this one

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:02.234
to make up their own minds."

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:05.534
He goes on to say, "I am
therefore proud to announce

00:07:05.534 --> 00:07:09.467
Eric has my complete
and total endorsement."

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:12.868
-That's right. There were two
guys named Eric in the race,

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.901
and Trump was too cowardly
to pick one.

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:17.567
So he just endorsed Eric,

00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:19.767
left it up to voters
to decide which one,

00:07:19.767 --> 00:07:22.100
and when one of the Erics won,
Trump claimed victory.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.968
It's like going
to the racetrack,

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:25.434
walking up
to the betting window,

00:07:25.434 --> 00:07:29.767
and saying, "I'd like to put
all my money on horse."

00:07:29.767 --> 00:07:31.400
You can't go back to the window

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.901
and claim victory
when a horse wins.

00:07:32.901 --> 00:07:34.534
Although, you know Trump
has done that.

00:07:34.534 --> 00:07:38.467
When he plays craps, he probably
says, "Show me dice."

00:07:39.701 --> 00:07:42.133
In fact, even Trump's own allies
were split

00:07:42.133 --> 00:07:44.467
on which Eric had gotten
the coveted Trump endorsement,

00:07:44.467 --> 00:07:47.300
with Ted Cruz tweeting that
Trump had endorsed Schmitt

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.901
and Rudy Giuliani tweeting,

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.634
"Missouri, get out and vote
for Eric Greitens,"

00:07:50.634 --> 00:07:53.567
with a photo that said,
"President Trump endorses
Eric Greitens."

00:07:53.567 --> 00:07:55.701
Although I'm just shocked
Rudy picked one of the Erics

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:57.167
who was actually running
and not a third,

00:07:57.167 --> 00:08:00.234
completely unrelated Eric who
doesn't even live in Missouri.

00:08:00.234 --> 00:08:02.334
"Missouri, go out and vote
for the Eric

00:08:02.334 --> 00:08:03.834
who's been endorsed
by Donald Trump --

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:06.033
Eric Clapton.

00:08:06.033 --> 00:08:08.267
I'm a huge fan
because 'Wonderful Tonight'

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:10.968
was my wedding song
when I married my cousin."

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:13.267
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:18.834
I was worried, because they say
when you get COVID,

00:08:18.834 --> 00:08:21.067
you lose your taste
for cousin jokes.

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:23.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.033 --> 00:08:35.534
And by the way, this is all just
stuff that happened last night.

00:08:35.534 --> 00:08:37.934
Usually July and August
are quiet months in politics,

00:08:37.934 --> 00:08:39.834
but a lot of crazy [bleep]
has been happening lately.

00:08:39.834 --> 00:08:42.467
And because we've been off for
a week, I missed a lot of it.

00:08:42.467 --> 00:08:44.200
In fact, I don't have time
to get to the rest of it.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.901
So to recap
as quickly as possible,

00:08:45.901 --> 00:08:47.701
I'm going to have to try out
a new segment called

00:08:47.701 --> 00:08:50.267
"Seth Recaps What He Missed
as Quickly as Possible."

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:53.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:55.501
Ready? Here we go.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.133
The Justice Department
is looking at

00:08:57.133 --> 00:08:58.701
Donald Trump's actions
as part of his investigation

00:08:58.701 --> 00:08:59.968
of the coup attempt
on January 6th.

00:08:59.968 --> 00:09:01.300
Trump is preparing
a legal defense

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:02.767
and looking for a fall guy.

00:09:02.767 --> 00:09:04.434
He also said no one's gotten
to the bottom of 9/11 yet.

00:09:04.434 --> 00:09:05.868
Matt Gaetz was caught
on a hot mic

00:09:05.868 --> 00:09:07.501
assuring indicted
Trump associate Roger Stone

00:09:07.501 --> 00:09:08.834
that he would get
a presidential pardon.

00:09:08.834 --> 00:09:10.567
The Department of Homeland
Security raised suspicions

00:09:10.567 --> 00:09:12.734
by hatching a plan to recover
deleted Secret Service texts

00:09:12.734 --> 00:09:14.167
from the day
of the attempted coup.

00:09:14.167 --> 00:09:16.367
The Pentagon also deleted
text messages from January 6th.

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:18.067
The U.S. killed al Qaeda's
leader in Afghanistan.

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:19.200
Nancy Pelosi went to Taiwan,

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.033
prompting a possible crisis
with China.

00:09:21.033 --> 00:09:23.200
Majority of House Republicans
voted against bills to codify

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.434
legal same-sex marriage and
contraception into federal law.

00:09:25.434 --> 00:09:27.200
Joe Manchin and Chuck Schumer
announced a deal out of nowhere

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:29.200
to pass a major piece of the
Democrat's domestic agenda,

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:30.734
including climate talks
and healthcare.

00:09:30.734 --> 00:09:32.100
Joe Biden tested positive
for COVID again,

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.801
and Ted Cruz was seen
fist-bumping a colleague

00:09:33.801 --> 00:09:35.467
on the Senate floor
after blocking a bill

00:09:35.467 --> 00:09:38.033
to fund healthcare for veterans
exposed to toxic burn pits

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:40.667
like they had just done a keg
stand at a Sigma Chi toga party.

00:09:40.667 --> 00:09:42.501
This has been "Seth Recaps
What He Missed

00:09:42.501 --> 00:09:44.133
as Quickly as Possible."

00:09:44.133 --> 00:09:46.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:53.868 --> 00:09:56.734
I had COVID, dude.

00:09:56.734 --> 00:09:58.934
I had COVID, dude,
and you wrote that?

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.834
I can't believe
they made me do that

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.000
immediately after recovering
from COVID.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.200
That's like if Joey Chestnut

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.667
had to do
the hot-dog-eating contest

00:10:05.667 --> 00:10:08.734
the day after
he got food poisoning.

00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:11.167
And, yes, it is true that I just
got back from a week off

00:10:11.167 --> 00:10:12.767
after getting COVID
a second time,

00:10:12.767 --> 00:10:14.167
or, as we call that
in show business,

00:10:14.167 --> 00:10:15.667
a season to pick up,

00:10:15.667 --> 00:10:20.467
which means I wasn't here
to comment on any of that.

00:10:20.467 --> 00:10:21.934
I couldn't even do shows
from my house

00:10:21.934 --> 00:10:23.868
because Biden asked
if he could borrow it.

00:10:23.868 --> 00:10:25.367
And...

00:10:27.033 --> 00:10:28.968
He went to high school
with the sea captain.

00:10:28.968 --> 00:10:32.834
I just want to say...

00:10:32.834 --> 00:10:36.067
I just want to say to all of you
out there who,

00:10:36.067 --> 00:10:38.634
upon learning that I had COVID,
immediately asked,

00:10:38.634 --> 00:10:41.901
can Wally host the show
while you're out?

00:10:41.901 --> 00:10:45.300
Thank you so much
for your concern.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:46.901
Although, if you ask me,
it's a little suspicious

00:10:46.901 --> 00:10:48.601
that all the tweets asking Wally
to guest host

00:10:48.601 --> 00:10:51.901
came from a Twitter account
named NotWally12345.

00:10:51.901 --> 00:10:53.334
-Sounds legit to me, Seth.

00:10:53.334 --> 00:10:54.400
-Does it?

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.667
-Yeah.

00:10:55.667 --> 00:10:57.501
[ Laughs ]

00:11:00.234 --> 00:11:03.067
-Last night was both
a promising sign of progress

00:11:03.067 --> 00:11:06.000
in the fight to safeguard
abortion rights on the one hand

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.767
and also a perfect case study

00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:09.467
of what the GOP has become
on the other hand.

00:11:09.467 --> 00:11:11.467
Voters in Kansas
overwhelmingly rejected

00:11:11.467 --> 00:11:13.667
the extremist views
of anti-abortion conservatives.

00:11:13.667 --> 00:11:15.300
Meanwhile,
pro-Trump candidates

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.067
won GOP primaries
throughout the country,

00:11:17.067 --> 00:11:19.601
even in places where Trump
endorsed multiple people.

00:11:19.601 --> 00:11:22.234
They all scrambled pathetically
to claim his endorsement.

00:11:22.234 --> 00:11:24.434
Republicans are still desperate
for the backing of any Trump

00:11:24.434 --> 00:11:26.734
they can get, whether
it's Donald Trump himself,

00:11:26.734 --> 00:11:29.601
Don Jr. or Ivanka,
just as long as it's not...

00:11:29.601 --> 00:11:30.601
-Eric.

00:11:30.601 --> 00:11:33.200
[ Laughter ]

00:11:34.434 --> 00:11:36.467
-This has been "A Closer Look."

